{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is scored exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement. Context data variables `J`, `N`, and `county` are used only as sizes/indices/predictors. All parameters have explicit built-in prior sampling statements before the likelihood uses transformed quantities depending on them.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> J;
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  vector[J] et;
  real mu_eta;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_eta;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_y;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[J] eta;
  vector[J] eta_adj;
  real mean_eta;
  real mu_adj;
  vector[N] y_hat;

  eta = 100 * mu_eta + sigma_eta * et;

  mean_eta = mean(eta);
  mu_adj = mean_eta;
  eta_adj = eta - mean_eta;
  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = eta[county[i]];
  }
}
model {
  mu_eta ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_eta ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);
  et ~ normal(0, 1);

  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":3,"N":1,"county":[1],"y":[1.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
